TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress — launch/orbit/ground control tasks planned but no applied course material (orbits, coverage) demonstrated yet"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress — 'Running basic simulations in STK will also be useful'; STK Design & Simulations tasks"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1 — Gantt chart with weekly tasks and deadlines"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Useful Links section plus footnoted sources"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress — STK tutorials 1–4 and background research completed, but no technical results shown"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"Claims near-real-time relay without discussing orbit/coverage implications (e.g. LEO revisit gaps vs GEO); feasibility not yet addressed."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"No contingency/slack provision in the Gantt chart for project variations."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"Preliminary progress lacks any quantitative technical work (no orbit parameters, coverage, or link budget estimates)."}],"overall":"Strong mission concept and rationale for an Australian reef-monitoring satellite with good referencing and a detailed Gantt-chart plan. Preliminary technical progress is limited to tutorials and reading, and the plan lacks contingencies; presentation is clean and professional.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":9.0,"scale":10.0,"points":36.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Clear mission purpose (GBR bleaching monitoring), explicit users (marine/conservation scientists), strong need justification with statistics and four cited literature sources. Slightly light on formal requirements/objectives, but well within Accomplished.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Reef-monitoring satellites could also be used to report sea surface temperatures, thermal stress on coral, and bathymetry"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":21.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"Detailed Gantt chart with week-by-week tasks, deadlines and narrative tying each task to the mission (launch, orbit, ground control, comms, end of life). However, no explicit contingency provision for project variations, keeping it at the lower Accomplished bound.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart. Detailed task descriptions can be found on the next page."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"The goal is to brainstorm and research as many possible strategies for the satellite’s launch/orbit and then gradually cut and refine them"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":5.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Progress is mostly background reading and STK tutorial completion; no preliminary technical results (no orbit, coverage, or link calculations) are presented or interpreted. On track, but work shown is minor rather than a good preliminary result set.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have read the brief of Asner’s monitoring system in Hawaii, researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity, and also completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":14.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Clear structure, well-written, consistent formatting, labelled Gantt figure with legend explained in text. Footnoted URLs match in-text citations. Minor issues: 'Useful Links' section is uncited in text and bare URLs rather than formatted references; report is short of typical depth.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Oceans have become 30 percent more acidic since the industrial revolution leading to the bleaching of coral reefs.¹"},{"where":"Useful Links","quote":"https://coralreefwatch.noaa.gov/satellite/publications/nim_skirving_reef_vulnerability.pdf"}]}]}
